# fstab — Libre Computer Le/La Frite (Amlogic arm64) light desktop.
#
# The boot media varies by board + flavor (La Frite: SPI u-boot + USB/eMMC root,
# NO microSD slot; Le Potato: microSD/eMMC). Unlike the RPi5 image, the Frite
# builder's .img files are LIVE / INSTALLER MEDIA (an MBR + one FAT32 partition
# carrying extlinux, the kernel, the FDT and a squashfs — build_frite_medium in
# build-frite-stage4.sh), never a disk image of the installed system: this fstab
# is largely inert on a live boot (/ is the live overlay). The INSTALLED system's
# layout is made by install-frite.sh AT INSTALL TIME: it partitions the target
# eMMC/SD (p1 FAT boot, p2 ext4 or LUKS2 root) and rewrites the two LABEL=
# device columns below to the PARTUUID/UUID of what it actually wrote, so the
# installed system mounts the right partitions whatever mmcblkN the eMMC is.
# The two LABEL= lines are the installer's sed anchors (^LABEL=FRITE_BOOT and
# ^LABEL=FRITE_ROOT, one line each): keep them first in their line, unindented,
# and keep exactly one of each — tests/scripts/test-frite-install-layout.sh pins
# that. The placeholder device paths are replaced at install time; do not rely on
# them literally.
#
# <device>         <mount>  <type>   <options>                              <dump> <pass>
LABEL=FRITE_BOOT   /boot    vfat     defaults,noatime,nosuid,nodev,noexec   0      2
LABEL=FRITE_ROOT   /        ext4     defaults,noatime                       0      1
tmpfs              /tmp     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,noexec,size=128m 0      0
tmpfs              /run     tmpfs    defaults,nosuid,nodev,mode=0755        0      0

# zram swap is configured at first boot by the builder's zram helper (the 512 MB
# SKU benefits from it). See build-frite-stage4.sh + RUNNING.md (SKU note).
